{"lines":[{"c":1,"h":0.021173736113113906,"x":0.84666855402203811,"y":0.047774755113896283,"t":"Reading","w":0.071585922241210964},{"y":0.098837209367436007,"h":0.015988371937820545,"w":0.11591695149739578,"c":1,"x":0.49826989786857079,"t":"READING"},{"h":0.016159251155012377,"c":1,"y":0.1742477255061341,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","w":0.2595155588785808,"x":0.19550173604572721},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","y":0.21063680920889916,"h":0.02046784160018722,"w":0.70415227254231771,"x":0.19550171848245773,"c":1},{"h":0.017615790797581354,"w":0.14359862009684243,"t":"Passage 1 below.","y":0.23093072109647705,"x":0.19550172791031845,"c":1},{"y":0.27034883775680607,"x":0.20761244770184872,"w":0.69723185221354167,"t":"The problems and benefits created by the spread","c":1,"h":0.027761728968797139},{"t":"of the water hyacinth in Kenya","y":0.30230930710810922,"w":0.4290657552083334,"h":0.026242127361791545,"c":1,"x":0.34256054790175766},{"x":0.19550173488252567,"w":0.6937716166178387,"c":1,"y":0.34593023227576736,"h":0.017610705424389583,"t":"Water hyacinth (Eichhornia crassipes), an aquatic plant native to South America, first"},{"c":1,"w":0.70948506673177092,"h":0.02001017803408367,"t":"appeared in countries in Africa in the early 1900s. Scientists there called it the 'world's","x":0.19542415826972595,"y":0.36237666535129964},{"y":0.38165798876900037,"w":0.68527460734049472,"h":0.021627962714396043,"x":0.19543311999784435,"c":1,"t":"worst aquatic weed', after it spread from the southernmost tip of Africa in the early"},{"y":0.39958012617212235,"w":0.44117645263671867,"t":"1900s and started obstructing major dams and rivers.","x":0.19550173903881926,"h":0.020643806857942648,"c":1},{"w":0.71107264200846354,"c":1,"x":0.19377163739667139,"t":"In east Africa the plant arrived with Belgian colonists in Rwanda, who liked the look of","h":0.019026559411937094,"y":0.43736878939165735},{"y":0.45486354107156923,"w":0.72145329793294277,"x":0.19377162097511094,"t":"its glossy leaves and delicate purple flowers floating in their ponds. But by the 1980s, it","h":0.018973668193883797,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.71288874308268224,"y":0.47374159524560444,"t":"had 'escaped' out of the country via the Kagera river and made its way downstream to","h":0.01894119922058668,"x":0.19545213913157605},{"y":0.49265220459971437,"c":1,"t":"Lake Victoria. There, with no natural predators and perfect temperature conditions, the","h":0.018975702343160594,"w":0.71799306233723958,"x":0.19550173865790366},{"x":0.19550172415558714,"w":0.70588236490885414,"t":"plant began spreading in the open water, blocking fishing routes and providing a new","y":0.51014695560907841,"c":1,"h":0.018922811792479122},{"t":"habitat for disease-carrying mosquitoes.","w":0.33391003926595053,"h":0.018923828867117409,"x":0.19550172769328791,"y":0.52904128737369982,"c":1},{"y":0.56242565401670053,"t":"For the women who smoke fish from the lake to sell it has meant declining income,","w":0.68531422932942709,"h":0.02192626723549107,"x":0.19541512881253234,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.7041522725423176,"t":"as the boats that once brought the fish to shore by the hundreds struggle to navigate","x":0.1955017183544272,"y":0.58430232560862638,"h":0.018916708677277239},{"y":0.60319767413669712,"c":1,"x":0.19377161961377246,"t":"through the mass of plants. But water hyacinth isn't their only headache. In order to","w":0.69031143188476562,"h":0.017516111476676643},{"h":0.018968582820692137,"c":1,"w":0.7179930623372397,"y":0.62063953490377588,"x":0.19377163512553797,"t":"smoke the fish that they buy, they must gather huge quantities of firewood, sometimes"},{"w":0.69735483805338538,"c":1,"y":0.63766545110412509,"x":0.19544382058214771,"t":"walking as far as 10km each way to collect enough to complete their work. And each","h":0.021513491097324144},{"h":0.019020456296735211,"c":1,"w":0.65916956583658859,"t":"day as they cook, they breathe in the thick, grey smoke. About three out of four","y":0.65697674421271313,"x":0.19550172223877665},{"t":"tamilies in Kenya depend on wood or charcoal to cook their daily meals, and the rate","c":1,"h":0.019964254177726182,"y":0.67519807732262471,"w":0.70079752604166667,"x":0.19372143912021708},{"w":0.67659723917643233,"h":0.02003424679840915,"y":0.69359679800334373,"c":1,"x":0.19369690988579349,"t":"is even higher in rural areas, Kenya's latest demographic and health survey shows."},{"h":0.015988371937820434,"t":"Using solid fuels like these for cooking increases indoor pollution. The World Health","x":0.19723183924012838,"y":0.71366279064203941,"w":0.68685119628906244,"c":1},{"h":0.021938231877299597,"y":0.72943931924803052,"t":"Organization estimates that about 14,300 Kenyans die annually as a result of indoor air","w":0.71468434651692714,"x":0.1954386015256272,"c":1},{"y":0.74842547224694056,"x":0.19550172546381095,"h":0.019016387998181838,"c":1,"t":"pollution - most of which is caused by cooking and heating sources.","w":0.56055363972981775},{"t":"Some years ago, on the shores of Lake Victoria, huge piles of water hyacinth that","h":0.021258402905153795,"y":0.78438065014988867,"c":1,"x":0.19544724380994202,"w":0.66793472290039058},{"t":"villagers had taken out of the water in an attempt to clear it were a common sight.","y":0.80370888733052115,"w":0.6799307759602865,"h":0.017512043178123271,"x":0.19550173999648091,"c":1},{"w":0.69908070882161455,"c":1,"y":0.82189225153262291,"t":"But buried in those decaying waxy leaves was a renewable energy gold mine. It turns","h":0.02043190029136277,"x":0.19544884629846934},{"x":0.19550173776257329,"y":0.8400979703899959,"h":0.018913657453362154,"c":1,"t":"out the floating plant isn't just good at spreading - its foliage also contains a high","w":0.67128026326497403},{"t":"ratio of carbon to nitrogen. It's a magic combination that has captivated researchers'","w":0.69926035563151034,"y":0.85603687591810029,"x":0.19365169266068391,"c":1,"h":0.023906857254957226},{"h":0.017494751574527623,"c":1,"y":0.87788663430223257,"t":"imaginations since as early as the 1980s when, across the world, they began to explore","w":0.71626296997070316,"x":0.19377162912131229},{"h":0.018926880091032494,"w":0.70069203694661453,"x":0.19377162858021998,"y":0.89534883722106184,"c":1,"t":"its potential as a biofuel. Just about 4kg of the dried plant would be enough to cater"},{"c":1,"y":0.91424418607325775,"t":"for a large family's daily energy needs, early research predicted.","x":0.19377161603283799,"w":0.52768168131510418,"h":0.018925863016394207},{"c":1,"t":"81","x":0.89273356421882799,"y":0.95203488379058654,"w":0.020761245091756142,"h":0.013081395100512871}],"w":2400,"h":2857}